Magic resistance does not protect against disintegration blasts from a
black dragon. However, being disintegration-resistant (e.g. from having
eaten another black dragon) will protect you and your armor.

Reflection is also useful to protect your rings and wands. In fort
Ludios, it is quite common for one or two of the soldiers to have
wands of lightning, and there could be blue dragons too. Being shock
resistant does _not_ protect your inventory from lightning effect.

(This means that the first black dragon is scary, but subsequently blue
dragons are more to be feared. Also, Mjollnir is inefficient on blue
dragons.)


